WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.991
The plan separates user payments, free points, and sponsor prize contributions.

00:00:06.021 --> 00:00:10.101
Each money flow has its own purpose, accounting record, and operating rule.

00:00:10.131 --> 00:00:15.165
This separation is the starting point for product, accounting, and legal design.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:20.097
Sponsors may provide contributions reserved solely for planned prizes.

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:25.578
Management reports separate sponsor funds. Financial reporting follows each contract.

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:30.707
We will reward winners only after completing legal and operating review in each country.

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:34.883
Current operating revenue is zero because the service has not launched.

00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:40.186
Our initial revenue plan has two sources: preservation support and referral fees.

00:00:40.216 --> 00:00:44.865
Advertising placement fees, licensed cards, and data services are later options.

00:00:44.965 --> 00:00:49.749
Sponsor advertising quizzes are the only initial source of free wallet points.

00:00:49.779 --> 00:00:54.973
Regular IP quizzes create a competition score. They do not add points to the wallet.

00:00:55.003 --> 00:00:59.717
Points are not sold, transferred, cashed out, or exchanged for external value.

00:00:59.817 --> 00:01:04.381
The initial support pieces are commemorative items, not officially licensed cards.

00:01:04.411 --> 00:01:07.699
Official digital cards require an IP license first.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:13.519
Paid card resale is undecided. It requires rights-holder consent and legal review.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:17.987
The prototype is designed to record quiz and advertising response events.

00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:22.387
Any service use requires notice, consent, security, and privacy controls.

00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:27.761
Partners would receive aggregated trends, not identifiable personal histories.

00:01:27.861 --> 00:01:32.431
The company plans to test human-run quizzes before adding AI assistance.

00:01:32.461 --> 00:01:37.112
For licensed titles, AI assistance would prepare draft questions.

00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:42.583
Before publication, people will verify rights, facts, wording, and translation.

00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:47.415
Seed is intended to test one complete sequence from acquisition to repeat use.

00:01:47.445 --> 00:01:52.484
It also tests sponsor participation, support purchases, and referral fees.

00:01:52.514 --> 00:01:58.732
The result must guide the next financing decision. Only a proven cycle should receive expansion funding.
